# title: Digital call (cash-or-nothing)
# category: Vanillas and digitals
# underlyings: 1
# source: Reiner & Rubinstein, Unscrambling the Binary Code, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: Pays a fixed amount if the stock ends above the strike, nothing otherwise.
# param: strike = 1.0 | percent | Strike, % of the initial level
# param: payout = 100 | amount | Cash paid if above the strike
#
# A hard threshold makes the Monte-Carlo delta noisy: tick Fuzzy to smooth it.

2027-01-04
    strike = 1.0
    payout = 100
    s0 = spot()

2028-01-04
    if spot() > strike * s0 then pays payout endIf
